    <body>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial,helvetica,sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;New Weekly Release Update:&lt;/b&gt; Click on the &lt;a href=&quot;http://salescrm.intel.com/ww43-updates/&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;What&amp;#39;s New&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt; section in Sales CRM to see the current weeks release update.  Additional training details are included.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;The 6 Quarter Product Schedule (6QPS) will be available in Salesforce on Thursday October 26&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;/sup&gt;.  This new functionality targets DCG Cloud and Communication Service Providers (CSP) Account Teams. We are piloting it with a few selected accounts, that will be contacted directly by DCG operations.&lt;/b&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;6 Quarters Product Scheduling in Sales CRM (Salesforce) provides ramp up data used by the Cloud Tracker Tool (CTT) to manage the DCG Cloud business. Today Account Executives, with CSP opportunities, have to use both Sales CRM and CTT to track their pipeline.  This enhancement provides a simple way for Field Sales to enter the first 6 quarters of product ramp data directly in the Sales CRM opportunity.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;For all others, it is not mandatory to use the new 6QPS. This section can be minimized by just one click on the header.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;                          &lt;img alt=&quot;User-added image&quot; src=&quot;https://shnintelqaconcs45crm.intelqa.shnpoc.net/servlet/servlet.ImageServer?id=015q00000006yGL&amp;amp;oid=00Dq0000000Blwx&amp;amp;lastMod=1508913537000&quot;&gt;&lt;/img&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;More information, &lt;a href=&quot;https://soco.intel.com/docs/DOC-2392222&quot;&gt;Trainings&lt;/a&gt; and additional communications can be found at &lt;a href=&quot;https://soco.intel.com/groups/cloud-crm&quot;&gt;SMG Sales CRM&lt;/a&gt; Inside Blue group.&lt;br&gt;For any additional questions, please contact &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:parsa.naderi@intel.com&quot;&gt;Parsa Naderi.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</body>
